    "text": "Here's the implementation of the function `can_arrange(arr)`:\n\n```python\ndef can_arrange(arr):\n    \"\"\"\n    Return the largest valid index of an element which that is greater than or equal to the element immediately preceding it.\n    no such element exists, return -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] <= arr[i - 1]:\n            return i\n    return -1\n```\n\nThis function iterates through the array starting from the second element and and checks if the current element is greater than than or equal to the previous element. If such an element is found, it returns the index of that element. If no such element is found, it returns -1.",
